monocypher 4.0.2 — vendored from
https://monocypher.org/download/monocypher-4.0.2.tar.gz
sha256 38d07179738c0c90677dba3ceb7a7b8496bcfea758ba1a53e803fed30ae0879c

License: BSD-2-Clause OR CC0-1.0 (we use BSD-2-Clause; see LICENSE.txt).
The combined statically-linked bash binary is GPL-3+ derivative work
(per binhex precedent); BSD-2 is GPL-3+ compatible — no license conflict.

Refresh procedure when bumping versions:
    1. Download new tarball from https://monocypher.org/download/
    2. tar xzf, then:
        cp src/monocypher.c   scripts/loadables/_monocypher/
        cp src/monocypher.h   scripts/loadables/_monocypher/
        cp LICENCE.md         scripts/loadables/_monocypher/LICENSE.txt
    3. Update the version + sha256 in this file.
    4. Re-run RFC 8032 KAT test (tests/bash-os/08-bashcrypto-ed25519.sh).

Files used by bash-os:
    monocypher.c    — implementation (~3 KLoC)
    monocypher.h    — public API (~300 lines)
    LICENSE.txt     — upstream LICENCE.md verbatim

Files NOT used:
    src/optional/   — chacha20+poly1305 alternatives + ed25519-shake;
                      ChaCha20+Poly1305 is provided by the Stage 19
                      mbedTLS path, and standard SHA-512 Ed25519 is
                      sufficient.

The underscore prefix on this directory tells
scripts/patch-bash-loadables.sh to skip its file-glob loop —
monocypher is library code that bashcrypto.c #includes, NOT a
separate bash builtin.
